From: MoveCertificate contributors
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: use the AFBC-capable packed format for YU10 images

Diagnostics from patch 037 show pan_image_layout_init() failing for
PIPE_FORMAT_Y10U10V10_420_UNORM_PACKED with an AFBC modifier: pan_afbc_format()
has no AFBC mode for the native packed YUV format.  The panfrost GL path uses
PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10_420_UNORM_PACKED for DRM_FORMAT_YUV420_10BIT imports,
which maps to PAN_AFBC_MODE_YUV420_6C10.  Switch the opaque YU10 mapping to
that pipe format so the AFBC layout can be created.

--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_image.h
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ static inline enum pipe_format
 panvk_format_to_pipe_format(VkFormat fmt)
 {
    if (panvk_format_is_external_yu10(fmt))
-      return PIPE_FORMAT_Y10U10V10_420_UNORM_PACKED;
+      return PIPE_FORMAT_R10G10B10_420_UNORM_PACKED;
 
    return vk_format_to_pipe_format(fmt);
 }
